<%# A contest summary card — banner, slate, name, status, prizes/spots/fee,
    lock date, and (when it has one) the sash laid across its top-right corner.

    Locals:
      contest         the Contest.
      entry_count     the FIELD size — every entrant's confirmed entries. Passed
                      in so the card never triggers its own count query. The
                      card SUBTRACTS it (see contest_spots_left) rather than
                      printing it.
      my_entry_count  THIS VIEWER'S entries, which is what the sash reports.
                      Defaults to 0 for a signed-out reader.

    `relative` is load-bearing, not decoration: both the dim layer and the sash
    are absolutely positioned against this card, and the existing
    `overflow-hidden` is what clips the sash's rotated ends into a corner
    ribbon rather than letting them hang off the card. It also clips the
    banner's hover push (.tt-contest-card-banner) back into the card. %>
<% my_entry_count = local_assigns.fetch(:my_entry_count, 0) %>
<% sash = contest_sash_label(contest, my_entry_count) %>
<% spots_left = contest_spots_left(contest, entry_count) %>

<%# TWO SURFACES, AND WHICH ONE THIS CARD GETS IS THE POINT.

    A live contest takes `.card-hover .tt-contest-card` and answers the cursor
    — it lifts, brightens its border, and pushes into its own banner. A COMING
    SOON one takes the inert `.card`: same box, no reaction. The rail mixes both
    bands, and the dim layer alone only said "later" once the reader had already
    committed to the card. Neither is disabled — a coming-soon card still opens
    its contest page — the hover just stops advertising it as playable now.

    `data-contest-hover` is the seam that pairing is asserted on
    (test/views/contest_card_stats_test.rb); a class list is not, because
    `.card-hover` and `.card` share a prefix and every card matches a substring
    probe for the shorter one. %>
<% live = !contest.coming_soon? %>
<%= link_to contest_path(contest),
            class: "#{live ? 'card-hover tt-contest-card' : 'card'} flex flex-col h-full overflow-hidden relative",
            data: { contest_card: contest.slug, contest_hover: (live ? "lift" : nil) } do %>
  <% if contest.contest_image.attached? %>
    <%= image_tag contest.contest_image, class: "tt-contest-card-banner w-full h-36 object-cover", alt: contest.name %>
  <% else %>
    <div class="tt-contest-card-banner w-full h-36" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--color-primary-700), var(--color-primary-900))"></div>
  <% end %>

  <div class="p-5 flex-1">
    <% if contest.slate %>
      <p class="text-xs text-secondary font-medium mb-1"><%= contest.slate.name %></p>
    <% end %>

    <%# NO STATUS BADGE ON THE CARD, and no wrapping title.
        The rail holds only open and coming-soon contests
        (Contest.featured_order excludes settled and cancelled), so an "Open"
        pill on every card made the same claim about all of them while taking
        the width the NAME needs. What is not open carries the sash instead,
        which says it louder and costs the title nothing.

        `truncate` then guarantees ONE line for any name, however long — the
        card is a fixed 320/384px and the names are operator-typed, so no font
        size can promise this and only a hard single-line rule can. The full
        name rides in `title` so a clipped one is still readable on hover, and
        it is never the only place the name appears: both tables below print it
        in full. %>
    <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-heading truncate mb-3" title="<%= contest.name %>"><%= contest.name %></h2>

    <%# The money line, in the order a reader decides in: what is on offer, how
        much room is left, what it costs. Prizes lead and are the only green
        figure, the same hierarchy the contest page's own stats row uses
        (contests/_contest_header row 2) — bold VALUE, muted label after it.

        SPOTS LEFT, NOT ENTRIES TAKEN. The two are the same fact read from
        opposite ends, and only one of them is the reader's: "0 entries" on a
        contest nobody has found yet reads as "nobody wants this", where "3
        spots left" on that same contest reads as "get in". The field size is
        still printed in full (n/max) on the contest page itself, where a reader
        who is deciding has room for both halves.

        `flex-wrap` because the figures are operator-set and unbounded — a
        four-digit pool beside a two-digit field is the widest this line gets,
        and it must break onto a second line rather than run under the card's
        rounded edge. %>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-3 gap-y-1 text-sm text-secondary mb-2" data-contest-money-line>
      <span class="whitespace-nowrap">
        <span class="font-extrabold text-primary"><%= dollars_short(contest.guaranteed_prize_dollars) %></span>
        <span class="text-xs text-muted">prizes</span>
      </span>
      <span class="text-muted">|</span>
      <span class="whitespace-nowrap">
        <span class="font-bold text-heading"><%= spots_left %></span>
        <span class="text-xs text-muted">spots left</span>
      </span>
      <span class="text-muted">|</span>
      <span class="whitespace-nowrap">
        <span class="font-bold text-heading"><%= dollars_short(contest.entry_fee_dollars) %></span>
        <span class="text-xs text-muted">entry</span>
      </span>
    </div>

    <% if contest.starts_at %>
      <p class="text-xs text-muted"><%= contest.starts_at.strftime("%b %-d, %Y") %></p>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <%# The not-ready-yet layer. It sits ABOVE the card's content and BELOW the
      sash, so the whole card reads as pushed back while the one label
      explaining why stays at full strength. `pointer-events-none` keeps the
      card clickable through it — a coming-soon contest is dimmed, not
      disabled, and clicking it opens the ordinary contest page. %>
  <% if contest.coming_soon? %>
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-black/40 pointer-events-none" aria-hidden="true" data-contest-dim></div>
  <% end %>

  <% if sash %>
    <div class="tt-sash <%= contest.coming_soon? ? "tt-sash-soon" : "tt-sash-entered" %>"
         data-contest-sash="<%= contest.coming_soon? ? "soon" : "entered" %>">
      <span><%= sash %></span>
    </div>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
